# Build-context excludes for Dockerfile.dev ONLY — BuildKit reads <Dockerfile>.dockerignore
# in place of .dockerignore, so the production image's .dockerignore is left as it is.
# The dev image COPYs pyproject.toml, uv.lock and the two dev scripts; the source arrives
# at runtime as a clone in the /workspace volume. So this keeps a local build's context
# small and secrets out of it. (infra builds from this repo's git URL, whose context is
# the tracked tree only.)

.git
.venv
.vscode/

**/__pycache__
*.pyc
*.swp
*.swo
.ruff_cache
.ropeproject

# Secrets and data, as .dockerignore keeps them out of the production build.
.env*
*.sql
